"""Build a practical, ID-preserving human validation guide."""
from pathlib import Path
import csv
from docx import Document
from docx.shared import Inches, Pt
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
d=Document(); sec=d.sections[0]
sec.top_margin=sec.bottom_margin=Inches(.65)
sec.left_margin=sec.right_margin=Inches(.75)
d.styles['Normal'].font.name='Calibri';d.styles['Normal'].font.size=Pt(11)
d.styles['Normal'].paragraph_format.space_after=Pt(7)
for st in d.styles:
 for border in list(st.element.xpath(".//w:pBdr")):
  border.getparent().remove(border)
def p(t):d.add_paragraph(t)
def h(t):d.add_heading(t,1)
def step(t):d.add_paragraph(t,style='List Number')
def page(t):d.add_page_break();h(t)
d.add_paragraph('Task 2: teammate setup and return guide','Title')
p('Group B | GPU sharing for multi-tenant inference | 16 October 2026')
h('Where we stand')
p('Cycle 1 recovery/audit is saved. Cycle 2 database reconciliation and workbook refresh are the current checkpoint. Cycle 3 screening has not started. The workbook is an interim evidence tracker, not proof of final inclusion.')
p('Current totals: 4,189 imported occurrences minus 111 duplicate links = 4,078 canonical records. Existing recommendations: 1,181 exclude and 1,066 retain/uncertain. Another 1,831 ScienceDirect records await their first recommendation. Five reports have 50 preliminary Q1-Q10 items and 26 outcome rows. Final decisions and final included-study count remain pending.')
h('Start here: no coding is required')
step('Open https://github.com/Raazia-Imran/os_CEPPPPPP and select main. Open task2/tracker/review_workbook.xlsx and click Download raw file. Open it in Excel or LibreOffice Calc. Download task1/submitted_protocol.pdf as the rulebook.')
step('Create a working copy named Eshaal_Task2_YYYY-MM-DD.xlsx or Rameen_Task2_YYYY-MM-DD.xlsx. Keep the original unchanged. Use one working copy throughout your batch.')
step('Click the required tab at the bottom. If tabs are hidden, use the sheet navigation arrows. Select the header row and enable Data > Filter. Filter only the assigned rows. Never sort a single column: sort the entire table so IDs stay with their evidence.')
step('Do not edit record_id, canonical_record_id, report_id or outcome_id. These IDs connect all tabs. Do not delete rows, rename headers, replace first-review judgments or enter your name for work someone else did.')
step('Read independently before comparing with preliminary judgments. Hide recommendation/reason or first score/rationale columns while forming your initial decision. Unhide them only after saving your own decision. Preserve disagreements for Raazia.')
p('An occurrence is one imported citation row; a canonical record is the deduplicated screening item; a report is one paper/version; a study is the underlying investigation. Two reports can describe one study. Do not count outcome rows as studies.')
page('Eshaal: independent screening, step by step')
step('Open Human validation. Filter priority to 1: 148 priority candidate records. Then continue the remaining assigned rows of the 1,066-candidate queue. The separate New import queue has 1,831 unscreened additions reserved for Cycle 3; it is not part of your existing validation assignment unless Raazia assigns it.')
step('Find the same record_id in Records. Read the title and actual abstract. Follow DOI or URL to the publisher if more text is needed. Search-result snippets are not complete abstracts. If the abstract is unavailable or the scope remains ambiguous, use uncertain and state what is missing.')
step('Decide whether the citation should proceed to full text. Enter independent_vote as retain (meaning include for full-text assessment), exclude, or uncertain. Retain is not final inclusion. For exclude, put the actual protocol EC code in criterion and add your independent explanation in a new independent_reason column. Do not overwrite the existing reason column.')
step('Add reviewer with your real name and fill checked_at_utc with the actual timestamp, for example YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ. If you only know local time, add checked_at_local and timezone=Asia/Karachi; do not label local time UTC. Add source_location with DOI/URL and abstract or page used. Keep final_decision pending for reconciliation.')
step('Open Exclusion sample. Check all 127 sampled records independently, using the same steps and independent_vote/criterion/reviewer/date/reason fields. A sampled false exclusion should be retain or uncertain with an explanation; do not change the original first recommendation.')
step('If existing ACM human decisions already exist, match them by DOI and then verify title/year against record_id. Preserve original reviewer/date in added original_reviewer and original_review_date fields. If a match is ambiguous, leave it unmatched and report the candidate IDs. Do not represent copied existing work as a new independent vote.')
p('Example of a reason format only: EC2; full abstract describes training exclusively and gives no separable inference result. Use this only when the cited record actually supports it. A title containing GPU alone does not prove eligibility.')
h('Return')
p('Return your full working .xlsx. Alternatively export Human validation as human_validation_queue.csv and Exclusion sample as exclusion_validation_sample.csv using CSV UTF-8. Excel exports only the active sheet: save each sheet separately and retain the full .xlsx. Keep every original column plus your new independent columns.')
page('Eshaal: recover the ACM search log')
step('Open Query audit and Export audit/Import manifest. The 79 numbered ACM files contain 1,582 occurrences. Two overlapping masters contain 829 and 1,000 entries; they are staged, not additive active imports. The claimed 1,600 hits and 1,603 exports have not been reconciled.')
step('Use saved search history, export history, notes or screenshots from the original operator. Record the exact accepted query, field, collection, filters, actual search date/time, timezone, displayed hits, export count and operator. Copy accepted syntax exactly. An upload date is not a search date.')
step('Create ACM_Run_Map in your copy, one row per original export filename. Use columns run_id, filename, query, field, collection, filters, search_date_time, timezone, displayed_hits, exported_occurrences, page_or_range, operator, evidence_location, mapping_status, notes.')
step('Map a numbered export to a run only when saved evidence supports it. Number 3 is absent among names 1-80, but that alone does not prove a missing results page. An overlapping master must not be added to the numbered-file total. Let the automated import compare identifiers and duplicates.')
step('For each unknown historical field write unknown and explain what evidence is missing. Do not rerun a search and call it the old run. If Raazia requests a new run, give it a new run_id and actual date, preserving the old evidence.')
p('The planned serving synonyms and pre-2020 MPS lanes must be compared with actual executed strings. Do not tick a planned search as complete because a related file exists. Return ACM_run_export_mapping.csv or the equivalent ACM_Run_Map tab, with original evidence locations.')
h('ScienceDirect discrepancy to preserve')
p('21 RIS files parse to 1,898 occurrences: API 41, MIG 241, MPS 563 and temporal 1,053. The MPS log reports 517 displayed hits but 563 exports. The temporal URL includes an open-access facet absent from the filter prose. Ask the original operator for evidence; do not alter counts to make them agree. Four represented databases do not establish complete search coverage.')
page('Rameen: obtain and assess the five reports')
step('Open Report validation: GB-P001 VastPipe, GB-P002 iGniter, GB-P003 gpulets, GB-P004 PipeSwitch, GB-P005 REEF conference. Locate each DOI/official link in Reference catalogue or Study extraction. Obtain the same final conference/journal version using the publisher, official proceedings or lawful author copy. University VPN may help if already configured; never share credentials.')
step('Save the paper privately with its report_id. Do not upload licensed PDFs to the public repository. Verify title, authors, venue, year and version. If the paper cannot be retrieved, log source URL, attempted date and access problem; report not retrieved is different from excluded.')
step('Read independently. In Full-text criteria, filter report_id and assess all IC1-IC6 rows for that report. Put pass, fail or uncertain in independent_vote, your name in checker and the real date in checked_at_utc. Add independent_anchor and independent_reason rather than overwriting the original source_anchor/first_review_basis.')
p('IC1: final English peer-reviewed primary conference/journal study. IC2: evaluated local GPU sharing among concurrent tenants/models/processes on one physical GPU. IC3: inference/model serving, with separable inference results for mixed workloads. IC4: inspectable relevant outcome and interpretable method/configuration. IC5: extractable within-one-GPU evidence and enough full text. IC6: main publication window or justified older exception. Consult protocol Tables 6-7 for the controlling wording.')
step('For a failure, propose the primary exclusion code using the protocol order: EC1 non-primary/non-peer-reviewed; EC2 no evaluable inference sharing; EC3 hardware-only; EC4 aggregate cluster/multi-GPU/remote-only evidence; EC5 non-GPU; EC6 insufficient available methods/outcomes; EC7 date/language. Do not use EC6 merely because a PDF could not be obtained.')
step('Complete checker and checked_at_utc in Report validation. Add independent_eligibility_vote and independent_reason; keep final_decision pending. Return Full-text criteria and Report validation tabs or fulltext_criteria.csv and report_validation_queue.csv.')
h('Two special checks')
p('PipeSwitch: locate exactly which experiments evaluate inference, whether inference results are separable from training, and whether they show concurrent co-tenant evidence on one physical GPU. Record page/figure plus IC3/IC5 reasoning. REEF: compare conference and journal titles/authors/experiments and publication statements. Record same-study/extended-report/distinct/uncertain with evidence. Do not replace the conference DOI with a journal DOI or merge reports automatically.')
page('Rameen: verify all 26 extracted outcomes')
step('Open Extraction and filter one report_id. Use outcome_id GB-O001-GB-O026 to track each check. Find source_anchor in the same PDF version. Record both PDF page and printed page if they differ, plus table/figure/section.')
step('Read the caption, surrounding text and experiment setup. Verify mechanism, GPU model/count, workload, batch size/request rate, co-tenants, baseline, metric, value, unit and statistic. Check whether a value is average, p95/p99, ratio, percent change or absolute measurement.')
step('Add independent_value, independent_units, independent_anchor, independent_conditions, independent_baseline and independent_note. Fill independent_checker and independent_checked_at_utc. Mark check_status with a clear result such as independent_agrees, correction_proposed or cannot_verify, retaining the original status in original_check_status if changing it.')
step('Never silently replace the first extracted value. Explain any proposed correction and calculation. A 2x throughput ratio is not a 200% increase. Mark missing information not_reported, not_extracted or cannot_verify as appropriate; zero is a measured value, not a missingness code. Graph estimates must be labelled estimates with the reading method.')
step('In Study extraction, check bibliographic identity, hardware/software, mechanism, workload, advantages, limitations and trade-offs against the report. Add independent notes and anchors. Do not infer isolation or energy benefits from throughput. Fill only evidence actually checked.')
p('Return extraction.csv and study_extraction_form.csv, or the equivalent tabs. Save after each report. A five-report check validates this pilot only; broader extraction for all eligible studies remains future work. The expected 15-20 studies is not permission to select papers to hit a number.')
page('Rameen: independently score Q1-Q10')
step('Open submitted_protocol.pdf quality-assessment section. Read the exact Q1-Q10 wording and 0-2 anchors before scoring. Open Quality, filter report_id and hide score/rationale while forming your initial score. Keep the rubric at hand; do not import the sample QA1-QA8 or Group A 0-1 scores.')
step('Assess all ten criteria for each of the five reports: 50 items total. Enter your score in second_score. Use 0, 1 or 2 according to the protocol anchors. Add independent_rationale and independent_anchor with the exact page/table/figure supporting the judgment.')
step('Use NA only where the protocol allows a justified not-applicable item; explain why and record its applicable maximum separately. Missing reporting is not automatically NA. Preserve original maximum and first score; Raazia will reconcile the applicable maximum and normalized score from actual decisions.')
step('Fill independent_checker and checked_at_utc. Keep reconciled_score blank and reconciliation_status pending until the independent results have been compared. Unhide first scores after saving yours; record disagreement without erasing either judgment.')
p('Applicable normalized score = sum of applicable scores / sum of applicable maxima. A fully applicable 10-item form has maximum 20. Below 60% informs sensitivity analysis; it is not an automatic exclusion. Return quality.csv or the Quality tab with all original and independent fields.')
h('Before sending your work back')
step('Check every completed row has its original ID, your actual name/date, an independent judgment, reason and source anchor. For unavailable evidence, state the precise limitation. Do not write checked against rows you did not inspect.')
step('Save and reopen the .xlsx. Confirm your tabs and entries remain present. Send the working file and a short note: completed IDs, unresolved IDs, proposed corrections and evidence needed. Screenshots can support an anchor but do not replace row-keyed return files.')
page('Raazia: reconcile returns and complete Task 2')
p('Automated work can maintain imports/hashes, compare IDs, flag inconsistent counts, build the workbook, compile diagrams/report and validate outputs. Teammates supply real independent judgments and historical evidence that has not been recorded. Do not ask them to duplicate already verified first-review automation.')
step('Keep each returned workbook unchanged as a reviewer snapshot. Join by record_id, report_id and outcome_id, not row number. Check duplicate IDs, missing IDs, changed source values and incomplete reviewer metadata. Compare independent judgments only after preserving them.')
step('Reconcile disagreements with reasons and actual participants/dates. Apply only justified identity links. Keep report versions and study relationships distinct. Recalculate all dependent totals from registers after accepted changes.')
step('Before submission, complete all remaining eligible-candidate screening, retrieval, full-text decisions, QA and extraction. Update PRISMA from actual decisions: identification, duplicates, screening, retrieval attempts/not retrieved, assessed exclusions by reason, reports and unique studies. Pending is not zero.')
step('Regenerate the PDF and workbook together, check references/anchors, and verify both open. The existing report PDF predates the ScienceDirect import and remains historical. Do not submit it as the current reconciled report.')
h('Heading 8-14 acceptance checklist')
for t in ['8 Search strategy: exact executed database/query table, fields, filters, dates, hits, exports, filenames, provenance and unresolved gaps; planned strings separate.','9 Literature period: actual per-run cutoff, 2026 publication-date checks and documented older-study exceptions.','10 Inclusion/exclusion: criteria tables and record/report-keyed independent and reconciled reasons.','11 PRISMA: traceable actual counts; unavailable reports separate from assessed exclusions; final reports and studies distinct.','12 Search/screening log: immutable IDs, database/title/year, duplicate links, first/independent/final decisions and reasons.','13 Quality: Group B Q1-Q10 scores, anchors, rationale, applicable maxima and sensitivity analysis.','14 Extraction: study identity plus outcome conditions, units, baseline, anchors, missingness, limitations and trade-offs for every eligible study.']:p(t)
p('Next cycle: Cycle 3 screening, duplicates and full-text decisions. Begin only when requested; Cycle 2 preparation does not supply those decisions.')
out=R/'task2/status_review/Task2_Detailed_Team_Guide.docx';d.save(out);print(out)
